 "notes": "38 screens on NIFTY futures 2023-01..2024-12 (1 lot, \u20b920/order, 1pt fut slippage, dated taxes). Ungated always-on intraday styles all lose: 15m Supertrend \u2212184k (t \u22123.2), VWAP cross+slope \u2212260k, ORB 30m \u2212174k, Donchian 30m \u2212132k, Keltner fade \u2212194k, W%R fade \u2212171k, BB fade \u221241k, gap go/fade, opening drive all negative; costs are ~4-5 pts/round trip and the faster signals have gross edge \u22640. Slower signals are ~breakeven (ST30 +22k, ST60 +30k, EMA9x21 30m +21k, all t<0.8, ex-top-k negative). Per-regime tables were mostly noisy and inconsistent across styles (e.g. ungated ST30 positive in calm regimes 1/3/5 and negative in volatile 4/6, but EMA30 the reverse); the only regime pattern repeated across variants was that daily-trend-aligned trend entries lose in regime 2 (up/volatile), n\u22485 each. The one thing that worked was aligning the intraday entry with the DAILY trend (1d close vs 1d EMA20): ST30 aligned +47.5k, PF 1.81, t 1.8, both years positive, survives 2\u00d7 slippage (+42k) and ex-top-k (+17.5k); 2024H1 was \u221213k. Alternative daily trend definition (1d Supertrend) +31k; EMA50 alignment \u22480; 15m \u221221k; 60m +7k, so the edge is real-ish only around 30m/EMA20. Pullback-in-trend variants: RSI15 \u221244k, BB15 +39k (t 0.75, ex-top-k \u221261k, profit all in regime 4 / 2024H2 \u2192 not submitted). ORB with daily alignment or after a narrow day still negative. Lot size changes (50\u219225\u219275) were handled by the engine; average net \u224817 pts/trade for candidate 1.",
 "platform_issues": [
  "spot_move_points is symmetric (exits on a move of N points either way), so on intraday futures it acts as both stop AND target. Directional intraday stops are only possible via combined.stop in points/rupees; exits.underlying_stop (ATR/trailing) is rejected for intraday specs ('applied in multi-day holding only'). An ATR-sized, one-sided, optionally trailing underlying stop for intraday would help trend strategies.",
  "exit_on_opposite_signal re-uses the full opposite entry condition, including any filters/gates in it (e.g. daily alignment), so with filtered entries it almost never fires; a separate neutral exit_signal is needed to express 'exit on opposite Supertrend flip'. Worth documenting.",
  "A handful of contract-day chunks missing in the snapshot for futures (missing_data 1-7 per 30m/60m screen in 2023-24), small."
 ],
